# "Delirium - This creature can't attack or block unless there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard"
# (CR 508.1c, 509.1b): Bot1's graveyard is empty, so in turn 3 Patchwork Beastie may not attack while Ornithopter is offered
# in the same declaration (the positive control), and in Bot2's turn 4 it may not block Curious Farm Animals while Ornithopter
# blocks it. Bot1 declines the upkeep mill ("you may"), so its library keeps its card.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Patchwork Beastie
Ornithopter
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Curious Farm Animals
Plains x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Patchwork Beastie.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Curious Farm Animals.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Decline
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Attack(Patchwork Beastie > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Curious Farm Animals > Bot1)
! Bot1.Block(Patchwork Beastie > Curious Farm Animals)
Bot1.Block(Ornithopter > Curious Farm Animals)
? Combat.Blocks = Ornithopter > Curious Farm Animals
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
Bot2.Battlefield.Curious Farm Animals.Damage = 0
